#{[17592186489261 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489142 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489261 #edb/ref 1069 "q-79264" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489261 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489261 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/df/dfcaa1de127881d7f6291efa2f78fbaecf1e5e29cea00d6b071c6ed2b800026f.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $g$ defined by the mapping diagram shown above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489261 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b6c7077f-943a-52fc-905d-553a194f631f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489261 #edb/ref 1074 "The range of $g(x)$ consists of all the outputs that have a corresponding $x$-input.\n\nIn a mapping diagram, the range consists of all the outputs to which an arrow is drawn.\n\nTherefore, the range is the set $\\{-\\frac{5}{2},0,2,6\\}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489284 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489057 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489284 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489081 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489284 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489097 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489284 #edb/ref 1069 "q-223598" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489284 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489284 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/e8/e874f46cd9a95c8bff5316128c72f4fd216194e44f54dc0929f6ad53a2e6a4c9.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?\n\n{{field-1}}\n$<\\,f(x)$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489284 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "eb6a9a5f-89b9-5986-bd3d-889c98bdbbd7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489284 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the lowest and highest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- The lowest $y$-value is $-4.$ This occurs at the point $(-4,-4).$ However note that this point is not actually included in the graph.\n\n- The highest $y$-value is $5.$ This occurs at the point $(4,5).$\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $-4$ and $5,$ including $5$ but not including $-4.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $-4<y\\le 5,$ which can also be written as $-4<f(x)\\le 5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489300 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489307 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489300 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "159ccee0-b33f-55fe-9d07-9d714f92c050" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489300 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489307 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489308 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489307 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2eb82c90-a1a8-520d-8355-fc0a5994a7b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489307 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489261 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489308 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489358 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489308 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "34ca2e15-f552-58af-9efe-ae01b771e8dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489308 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083936 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489347 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9e6f8517-e5f3-5c96-a470-bfc022e34808" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489347 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489284 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489358 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489358 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ba4b8236-b97b-5374-a353-33387e9cdd0a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489358 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489217 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
